-- title:
--   Diagonal norm strings over Kᵥ realise exactly pairs of local norms
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $L$ be number fields with $L$ an extension of $K$ that is finite and Galois, and let $\sigma$ be a $K$-automorphism of $L$ such that every $K$-automorphism $\tau$ of $L$ lies in the subgroup generated by the integer powers of $\sigma$ (so the Galois group is cyclic with generator $\sigma$). Let $v$ be a maximal ideal of $\mathcal{O}_K$, write $K_v$ for the $v$-adic completion of $K$ and $E = L \otimes_K K_v$, and let $a, b \in K_v^{\times}$. The assertion is an equivalence. On the left: there exist $\alpha, \beta \in E^{\times}$ such that the norm string of the diagonal element $\mathrm{diag}(\alpha,\beta) \in \mathrm{GL}_2(E)$ — that is, the product $\prod_{i=0}^{n-1} \sigma^{i}(\mathrm{diag}(\alpha,\beta))$ over $i < n = [L:K]$, where $\sigma$ acts entrywise on $\mathrm{GL}_2(E)$ through its action on the left tensor factor — equals the image of $\mathrm{diag}(a,b) \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_v)$ under the entrywise map induced by $K_v \to E$. On the right: $a$ is the $E/K_v$ algebra norm of some $\alpha \in E^{\times}$, and $b$ is the $E/K_v$ algebra norm of some $\beta \in E^{\times}$.
--
--   This identifies, for the split diagonal torus, the elements of $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_v)$ admitting a diagonal twisted-norm lift from $\mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K K_v)$ with those whose diagonal entries are local norms, the torus case of the norm correspondence in cyclic base change for $\mathrm{GL}_2$. It is used in the local analysis of twisted orbital integrals, in particular for the vanishing of split orbital terms when a matching element fails to be a norm, and for the corresponding neighbourhood and estimate statements.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AutomorphicForm_exists_normString_diagUnits2_eq_toTensorGL_diagUnits2_iff_exists_norm_eq.lean

